  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e86d087d1926473fbd585301bc64adf9, type: 3}
  m_Name: PostTip Data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  InterviewTips:
  - 'Use the STAR method to describe your achievements: Situation, Task, Action,
    Result. It turns vague claims into concrete proof.'
  - Tailor your CV to every job. Do this by making use of key words from their job
    descriptions. This will help you get past the AI screens so a human can then
    look at your application.
  - Networking is not just asking for favours. Build genuine relationships by sharing
    useful content, attending events, and offering help first.
  - Quantify your impact wherever possible. Instead of 'improved code quality,' say
    'reduced bugs by 30% through code reviews and automated testing.
  - A portfolio project often outweighs certificates. Build one small project that
    solves a real problem, document it, and put the link on your LinkedIn.
